    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e37251cf_712fe511",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-07T01:44:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we re-use \u0027apexd.status\u003dready\u0027 which tells we can use contents from apexes? In a normal Android, this is set by \u0027apexd --snapshotde\u0027, which is not run in vm mode.\n\nFor now, apexd --vm sets apexd.status\u003dready[1], but it seems to be right for init to set it after running \u0027perform_apex_config\u0027, not by \u0027apexd --vm\u0027\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:system/apex/apexd/apexd.cpp;l\u003d3396-3398?q\u003dapexd.cpp",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "428a96f871b4dba8603d40c9c9be67e8aac7e56e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e5773d5_fb39f563",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-07T05:15:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "apexd.status has been set by apexd. I don\u0027t think it\u0027s good to make an exception to that just to not introduce a new sysprop.",
      "parentUuid": "e37251cf_712fe511",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "428a96f871b4dba8603d40c9c9be67e8aac7e56e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20cfbd08_b3b4ecda",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-07T05:31:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO it would fix the current/wrong behavior of apexd setting apexd.status\u003dready even when APEXes are not ready to be used yet.",
      "parentUuid": "7e5773d5_fb39f563",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "428a96f871b4dba8603d40c9c9be67e8aac7e56e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3338ea0b_238643e8",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-07T05:44:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The meaning of apexd.status\u003dready has been clear. It means that APEXes are correctly mounted and can be accessed via the /apex paths [1]. Therefore, I don\u0027t think the current behavior is wrong. It does not mean that the extra steps like linkerconfig, etc. are done. Those steps themselves could be triggered from apexd.status\u003dready.\n\nIf someone wants to wait until the linkerconfig becomes ready, they should wait for the sysprop for the very event, not an event from apexd which might be an impl detail of linkerconfig.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:system/apex/apexd/apexd.cpp;drc\u003dmaster;l\u003d2945",
      "parentUuid": "20cfbd08_b3b4ecda",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "428a96f871b4dba8603d40c9c9be67e8aac7e56e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
